## 1. Product goal and vision (the owner's words, summarised)

Reminders in Panga are a **lightweight daily checklist with dates**. They are not a calendar app and not a server-backed alarm system.

- A reminder is something you **check**: you open Reminders and see **what is on today**. You might decide you don't care about some of it.
- You can also see **what you did not do** on earlier days. You go through those, **tick some off and leave others open**.
- A reminder is either a **plain reminder** (a day, no alert) or a **timed reminder** (a day plus a time, with an alert).
- **Ticking a reminder off deletes it.** You don't need to be reminded any more. (An Undo is offered for a few seconds.)
- A reminder can **repeat**: every day, every 2 days, every 3 days, weekly, monthly, yearly, "whatever". Ticking a repeating reminder finishes that occurrence and it comes back on its next date; it is not deleted.
- Reminders **cut across workspaces**: the same list everywhere.
- Events can be **imported from a Google Calendar export** (Google's zip or any `.ics` file) into this list.
- Alerts only need to work **while the app is open**. **There is no server, no Web Push and no background scheduling** (owner decision, final). Anything that came due while Panga was closed is simply there in Today or Overdue when the app is opened.

There is **no Google sign-in, no Google client ID, no Google API** in this work. Google integration was deliberately removed from the app earlier (rule dated 2026-11-22: remove every Google/Drive/Calendar reference). Import works purely from files the user exports themselves. Do not add any Google script, SDK, OAuth flow or CSP entry. Do not mention Google API keys anywhere in the UI.

**Keep it simple.** Features not in this vision (snooze, advance-notice offsets, "missed while closed" catch-up lists, server push) are intentionally **left out**. Do not add them.

