### 5.4 Row design and actions
Each row: a **checkbox** (the tick), the message, the time (timed only), a muted repeat summary (`Repeats every 2 days`), location if any, and the word `Imported` for imported items. Actions: `Edit`, `Delete`.

**Tick behaviour (the core interaction):**
- **One-time reminder:** ticking **deletes** it immediately and shows a toast `Done: <title>` with an `Undo` button for 6 seconds. `Undo` restores the exact same record (same id and fields). Implement by keeping the deleted row in memory for the toast's lifetime and re-inserting it.
- **Repeating reminder:** ticking **does not delete the series**. It completes this occurrence and moves the reminder to its next date per decision D7 (see 9.1 `nextAfterComplete`). Toast: `Done: <title>. Next: Thu 3 Dec` with `Undo` (restores the previous date). If no next occurrence exists (series ended by `until` or `count`), ticking deletes it like a one-time reminder.
- `Delete` on a one-time reminder removes it without ticking (confirm with `confirmDelete`). `Delete` on a repeating reminder removes the **whole series** and says so in the confirmation (`This reminder repeats. Delete it and all future repeats?`).

There is no snooze, no "skip this one" and no "end repeat" button: ticking covers skipping; Delete ends a series.

### 5.5 Alerts while the app is open
When a **timed** reminder's time arrives and Panga is open (any tab or page of the app):
1. Show an **operating-system notification** if permission is granted (see 9.2).
2. Always show an **in-app banner** at the top of the screen: `Reminder: <message>` with `Tick off` and `Dismiss`. `Dismiss` only hides the banner; the reminder stays open in Today (or Overdue tomorrow). `Tick off` behaves exactly like ticking it in the list. Several due at once stack in the banner area (max 3 shown, then `+2 more` linking to Today).
3. Each occurrence alerts **once** (remember `lastAlertedAt`).

If a timed reminder's time passed while Panga was closed, **no catch-up alert** is shown: it is simply listed in Today (or Overdue if it was an earlier day) when the app opens. Plain reminders never alert.

