## 6. Data model changes

### 6.1 New `Reminder` fields (all optional so old rows stay valid)
```ts
export type ReminderRepeatFreq = "daily" | "weekly" | "monthly" | "yearly";

export interface ReminderRecurrence {
  freq: ReminderRepeatFreq;
  interval: number;            // >= 1.  "Every 2 days" = { freq: "daily", interval: 2 }
  anchorAt: number;            // epoch ms of the series' first occurrence (the fixed schedule is computed from this)
  byWeekday?: number[];        // 0 = Sunday .. 6 = Saturday; weekly only
  byMonthDay?: number;         // 1..31; monthly only (default: day of anchorAt)
  until?: number;              // epoch ms, inclusive end of the series
  count?: number;              // total occurrences from anchorAt, including the first
  exdates?: number[];          // occurrence times (epoch ms) that are skipped (from imports)
}

export interface Reminder {
  /* existing fields unchanged: id, folderId, toneId, linkedEntityType, linkedEntityId,
     message, triggerAt, status, createdAt, updatedAt, syncStatus, userId */
  timed?: boolean;             // true = alerts at triggerAt. false = plain reminder (triggerAt is local 00:00 of the due day)
                               // IMPORTANT: legacy rows have timed === undefined and MUST be treated as timed (they always had a time)
  endAt?: number;              // optional event end (imports)
  location?: string;
  notes?: string;
  recurrence?: ReminderRecurrence | null;
  occurrencesDone?: number;    // counts toward `count`
  lastAlertedAt?: number | null; // the triggerAt value we last alerted for, so each occurrence alerts once
  workspaceId?: string;        // where it was created (display only, never a filter)
  source?: "manual" | "ics";
  externalUid?: string;        // iCalendar UID
  externalInstance?: string | null; // RECURRENCE-ID for a moved single occurrence
  externalSequence?: number;   // iCalendar SEQUENCE, for update detection
  externalModified?: number;   // LAST-MODIFIED as epoch ms
  rruleRaw?: string | null;    // original RRULE text, kept for transparency
}
```

Semantics to implement exactly:
- `triggerAt` is the reminder's **due moment**. For a timed reminder it is the date and time; for a plain reminder it is local midnight of the due day. The "due day" of any reminder is the local calendar day of `triggerAt`. Every existing query on `triggerAt` keeps working.
- A reminder with `recurrence` is **one row per series**. Ticking it (5.4) advances `triggerAt` to the next occurrence and increments `occurrencesDone`; it stays open.
- **Open vs done:** a row that exists is open. Ticking **deletes** the row (one-time) or advances it (repeating). New rows always have `status: "pending"`. Do not write `fired` or `dismissed` any more. Legacy `dismissed` rows are hidden from every view (decision D11); legacy `fired` and `pending` rows are shown as open. Never delete legacy rows in the migration.
- The reminder's date fields are always interpreted in the device's local time zone.

