## 13. Edge-case checklist (verify each in tests or in the stage report)
- Event starts at 00:00 local or ends at midnight; all-day events spanning several days (store as one reminder starting on the first day).
- The device time zone differs from the event's `TZID`; the owner is in Africa/Nairobi (UTC+3, no DST) but the code must be correct for DST zones.
- A series whose `UNTIL` is date-only vs date-time; `UNTIL` in UTC while the event uses `TZID`.
- `EXDATE` on a date that is not an occurrence (ignore silently).
- Duplicate UIDs across different calendar files in the same zip (Google sometimes repeats shared events): treat the same UID+instance as one; if details differ, the higher SEQUENCE wins.
- Importing the same file twice quickly (double click): disable the button while `importing`; the unique key logic must make a second run a no-op even if the first one is still finishing.
- Empty title, very long description, emoji in titles (keep as text; do not strip).
- Browser tab closed mid-import: chunked transactions mean a partial import is possible; the next import completes it safely thanks to the identity key.
- Notification permission revoked after being granted: the state check runs on every tab focus.
- Locale: format dates with `Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, ...)`; do not hard-code `en-US`.
- Accessibility: file input has a visible label; preview checkboxes have accessible names including the event title; `aria-live="polite"` on progress and result text; focus moves to the summary on `done`; the modal closes on Escape and returns focus to the trigger.
- Phone layout (Galaxy A07, ~360px wide): no horizontal scroll, 14px outer margin (`--gutter`), long titles wrap (`overflow-wrap: anywhere`), tap targets at least 44px.

