## 14. Don'ts
- No Google API, client ID, OAuth, `gapi`, GIS script, or network call to Google. No CSP changes for Google.
- No mock or sample reminders, no seeded data.
- No new dependency except `fflate` (approved in D2). State its exact version and licence in the PR.
- No deleting of legacy tables or rows. No hard-coded colours. No emojis in the UI.
- No server, no Web Push, no background sync, no snooze, no advance-notice setting, no catch-up/missed list. These were removed from scope by the owner.
- Do not change unrelated files, rename existing exports, or reformat files you do not need to touch.
- Do not weaken or delete existing tests to make them pass; update them only where behaviour intentionally changed, and say which and why.

